        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d4217279-5b7f-56b8-9b4b-4539932c75d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Plant, Phil Collins, John Bonham, Nika Boon, John Baggott, Ian Matthews, Jay Stapley, Carey Willetts, Carla Azar\n- Bands/Projects: Led Zeppelin, Massive Attack, Portishead, Kasabian, Pink Floyd, Mike Oldfield, Athlete, Future Perfect\n- Topics: Discography, tours, album collaboration, music review\n\nFacts:\n- John Bonham was born on 31 May 1948 and died on 25 September 1980.\n- John Bonham was an English musician and songwriter best known as the drummer for the British rock band Led Zeppelin.\n- Robert Plant avoided performing Led Zeppelin songs through much of the period described on his discography page.\n- Robert Plant's 1983 tour, which featured drummer Phil Collins, was very successful and often played to sold-out arena-sized venues.\n- Robert Plant's 1985 tour was very successful and often played to sold-out arena-sized venues.\n- Nika Boon was working on a new album planned for release in 2017.\n- Nika Boon's 2017 album project involved collaboration with John Baggott, Ian Matthews, Jay Stapley, and Carey Willetts.\n- John Baggott plays keyboards and Moog instruments for Massive Attack, Portishead, and Robert Plant.\n- Ian Matthews was identified as the drummer from Kasabian.\n- Jay Stapley was identified as a guitarist associated with Pink Floyd and Mike Oldfield.\n- Carey Willetts was identified as the bass player from the band Athlete.\n- A Pitchfork review of Future Perfect said that in the first 10 seconds of the album opener, Carla Azar outperformed most beat-makers with her \"Leibezeit-cum-Bonham\" percussion.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "45bcd6d2-6916-5cb1-9eb6-fda2eec0fe78",
        "text": "Page: Robert Plant discography. Sentence: Although Plant avoided performing Led Zeppelin songs through much of this period, his tours in 1983 (with drummer Phil Collins) and 1985 were very successful, often performing to sold-out arena-sized venues.\nPage: John Bonham. Sentence: John Henry Bonham (31 May 1948 – 25 September 1980) was an English musician and songwriter, best known as the drummer for the British rock band Led Zeppelin.\nPage: Nika Boon. Sentence: She is currently working on her new album (release 2017) in collaboration with musicians namely John Baggott (who plays keyboard & moogs for Massive Attack, Portishead, Robert Plant), Ian Matthews (drummer from Kasabian), Jay Stapley (guitarist associated with Pink Floyd and Mike Oldfield) and Carey Willetts (bass player from band Athlete).\nPage: Future Perfect. Sentence: A Pitchfork review stated, \"In the first 10 seconds of the album opener, Carla Azar shames most every beat-maker with her ridiculous Leibezeit-cum-Bonham percussion\".",
